      "created_at": "2020-03-16T18:24:48Z",
      "updated_at": "2020-03-16T18:25:49Z",
      "body": "First, thank you very much for your detailed answer.\r\n\r\nI understand that it is not easy to provide a hash mechanism strong enough for anonymization use case.\r\nAnd I understand that SHA2 is not really strong enough for anonymization use case.\r\n\r\nThat said, on a more global point of view, I think that it is very important to have a homogeneous filter/process offer between Logstash and Ingest Pipelines.\r\n\r\nI mean that I would find very sad to have fingerprint filter in Logstash and fingerprint processor in ingest pipeline with different options and behavior.\r\n\r\nThat's why a first step would be to provide fingerprint processor with same features and behavior than Logstash.\r\n\r\nAnd later, maybe a nice idea to have a strong anonymization hash will emerge :)",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
