      "created_at": "2020-06-22T11:50:56Z",
      "updated_at": "2021-02-09T12:17:37Z",
      "body": "From my understanding, we are talking about pseudonymization in the GDPR context here because even with the more suitable version of fingerprinting with a secret key (HMAC), users could still be re-identified with the knowledge of the secret key. Maybe add a way to rotate this key at defined intervals? This would provide strong pseudonymization properties after the rotation period. Note that this is just an idea. I have not checked if others are using such a design and what possible downsides are.\r\n\r\n\r\n> That's why a first step would be to provide fingerprint processor with same features and behavior than Logstash.\r\n\r\nNot sure that you would really want that as the Logstash fingerprint filter is currently non-stable/none-deterministic for nested fields. Ref: https://github.com/logstash-plugins/logstash-filter-fingerprint/pull/41",
      "author_association": "NONE",
